  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PNG Institute of Medical Research (PNGIMR) Institutional Strengthening (STRONGIM IMR) (Asia-Pacific)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Research and Operational Needs through Good Infrastructure and Modernisation will deliver institutional strengthening initiatives to the PNG Institute of Medical Research (PMGIMR). 
This investment will build on the five-year Indo Pacific Health Security Initiative (HSI) 2017-22 with a focus on:
-	infrastructure enhancements to encourage safe and productive workplaces.
-	modern IT improvements &amp; upgrades
-	strengthening the research workforce; and
-	fortifying administrative and support services. 
Additionally, the PNG Health Program supports a co-funding arrangement and will contribute an additional AUD $2,082,500 over 4 years to strengthen research on social, cultural, and behavioural factors affecting health and health equity in Papua New Guinea.</narrative>
  </description>
